  <prompt>🔴 DO NOT REORDER ANYTHING. THE REORDER ALREADY SHIPPED. This task was written to change `EntityCreationService` from upload→create→link to create→upload→link across 7 wizards. Task **076** did that, and the new contract is enforced by the TYPE SYSTEM, not by convention.

This task is now a CLOSE-OUT: retire three stale comments that still advertise work as pending, pin the shipped ordering with a regression test so it cannot silently revert, and re-home two residual items to the tasks that can actually discharge them.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE frontend engineer. Comment hygiene on a shipped cutover, plus one ordering regression test.</role>
  <goal>No comment in this repo still tells a reader that the create-first reorder is pending work belonging to this task; the shipped ordering is pinned by a test that fails if anyone reverts it; and the two items this task cannot discharge itself are recorded against the tasks that can.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 **ALL FOUR OF THIS TASK'S ORIGINAL PREMISES WERE FALSE AT HEAD.** Re-verified 2026-09-21 against the code, not against the plan note:

1. **"`EntityCreationService.ts` orders upload → create → link."** FALSE. The file's own usage example (`:27-31`) now reads: *"Create the record FIRST — the upload is keyed on it, and the server resolves the storage container from that same record (task 076). There is no container parameter."*

2. **Create-first is COMPILER-ENFORCED, which is stronger than "by convention".** `uploadFilesToSpe(entityLogicalName, recordId, files, onProgress?)` (`:479-484`) takes the record as a required parameter. The old `(containerId, files, onProgress)` shape cannot compile, so every un-migrated call site is a BUILD ERROR rather than a silent pass-through. There is no container parameter to get wrong.

3. **"The Secure Project step exists in TWO implementations."** FALSE — there is exactly ONE: `Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateProjectWizard/SecureProjectSection.tsx`. The `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace` copy was deleted in `144ef43c4` on **2026-09-01**; this task was filed **2026-09-03**, so it was BORN STALE. The escalation trigger about "both components being live" therefore cannot fire, and the 068 sequencing decision this task was told to make has no subject.

4. **"There are exactly three such flows."** FALSE — there are **TWO**. `uploadFilesWithoutRecord` has exactly two callers at HEAD (ripgrep over `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}`): `createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts:262` (EmailComposer local attachment) and `CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx:783` (Analysis wizard standalone document). The third — DocumentUploadWizard's "skip associate" — was cut over by task **076**.

**THE CLASSIFICATION CONFLICT, AND WHY IT IS NOT THIS TASK'S TO INVENT.** `EntityCreationService.ts:511-513` calls the two survivors debt: *"reordering them so the record exists first is task 093, after which this method should lose callers."* Task 076's own notes (`notes/task-076-client-cutover-and-supplier-classification.md:54-55`) classify BOTH as legitimately **"parentless"** — an email attachment on an unsent draft and a standalone analysis document have no record to belong to yet. Both cannot be right.

Two of three sources favour 076: its classification is later, it performed the cutover, and the comment is *demonstrably wrong about the count* (three vs two) in the same sentence. So the comment is the stale artifact. ⚠️ Record that reasoning explicitly and flag it for owner confirmation — do NOT present it as a decision this task made on its own authority.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts — the `uploadFilesWithoutRecord` doc comment (~:503-517): wrong count AND wrong attribution</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx — ~:772 "Reordering this wizard to create the analysis first is task 093."</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts — ~:247 "…removing the need for the record-less route at all — is task 093."</file>
      <file role="new">a jest test pinning create-before-upload in EntityCreationService (path per the package's existing __tests__ convention)</file>
