    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task-093 rescope 2026-09-21">🔴 SCOPE: do NOT reorder any wizard, do NOT change `EntityCreationService`'s ordering, and do NOT author or modify any Secure Project UI. All of that either shipped or never existed. Touching it re-opens a closed, compiler-enforced contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="measured 2026-09-21">🔴 COMMENT COLLISION — THE ONE REAL HAZARD IN THIS TASK. A repo-wide search for "task 093" returns ~24 hits, and **only THREE belong to this project**. The rest are same-numbered tasks in OTHER projects — `spaarkeai-compose-r1` task 093 (`LegalWorkspace/vite.config.ts`, `composeEditor.registration.ts`, `Spaarke.Compose.Components/**`, `ThreePaneShell.tsx`), SpaarkeAi's task 093 (`ManageWorkspacesPane.tsx`, `workspaceLayoutMutations.ts`, `workspaceTemplateFilter.ts`, `App.tsx`), and others. Task numbers are per-project and they COLLIDE. Edit ONLY the three files named in relevant-files. A blanket sweep would corrupt four other projects' records.</constraint>
    <constraint source="plan D-8">Scope: the classification. State 076's "parentless" reading as the resolution WITH its evidence, and flag it for owner confirmation. If the owner instead confirms the comment's "debt" reading, that becomes a NEW small task — it is not this one, and it must not be improvised in.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The new test goes at a KEEP path and must be a real regression pin: it fails if `uploadFilesToSpe` loses its record parameter or if a wizard calls upload before create. A test that merely restates the current signature is scaffolding, not a pin.</constraint>
    <constraint source="review-2026-08-24">Perturbation is mandatory: break the ordering the new test pins and confirm it reddens; then restore.</constraint>
    <constraint source="main-session ownership">Do NOT edit `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` or `current-task.md`; do not set this POML's own `&lt;status&gt;`. Do not touch anything under `.claude/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

